-- title:
--   Specialisation of j(qᵈ) as q-th power of cyclic-quotient invariant
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q \nmid M'$, and a prime $\ell_g$ with $\ell_g \equiv 11 \pmod{12}$ and $\ell_g \mid M'$.
--
--   **Valuation data over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and the supersingular package.** Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\mathrm{AlgebraicClosure}\ \mathbb Q$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. A finite set $W$ of places of the field $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ (\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)\ M' = (\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)(j_q^{\bmod}, j_q^{\bmod}(q^{M'}))$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ is given, with `hW` asserting that $W$ consists exactly of the places lying in $\mathrm{ssPlaces}\ q\ M'$, i.e. those satisfying the predicate `IsSupersingularPlace q M'`; `s` is a distinguished element of $W$. The hypothesis `hle` states the inclusion $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M' \le \mathrm{fieldBar}\ q\ M'$ of subfields of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}$, namely of the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-field generated by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field inside the one attached to level $q^2M'$ and the subgroup $\mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M'$. Here $\mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M'$ is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. Further, $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$ to $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ (\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A)\ M'$: a valuation subring of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, compatible with $A$ and with its residue map, together with a degree-preserving map on places compatible with orders of vanishing and divisors. The hypothesis `hR_0` requires this reduction to agree with coefficientwise reduction: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ \overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldBar}\ M'$, that element lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$.
--
--   **The local base.** Let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q \subseteq \overline{\mathbb Q}$ and put $A_0 := A \cap k_0$ (formally `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ (AlgebraicClosure ℚ))`). An element $\pi_0 \in k_0$ lying in $A$ is given, and the hypotheses `hdvr`, `hunif`, `hhens`, `hres` state that $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, that its maximal ideal is generated by $\pi_0$, that it is Henselian local, and that its residue field is algebraically closed; `hκ` states that every $a \in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to an element of $k_0$ lying in $A$.
--
--   **Roots of unity, level and the function field.** An element $\xi \in k_0$ is a primitive $(q\ell_g)$-th root of unity (`hξ`), and `hιξ` provides a ring homomorphism $k_0 \to \mathbb C$ sending $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell_g))$. The subgroup $H_1 \le (\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times$ is, by `hH₁`, the intersection of $\mathrm{levelH}\ q\ M'$ with the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times \to (\mathbb Z/\ell_g)^\times$. The field $K$ is, by `hK`, the $k_0$-subfield $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\ k_0\ (\mathrm{xHFunctionField}\ (q^2M')\ H_1)$ of $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k_0$, generated over $k_0$ by the coefficientwise image of the function field of the level-$(q^2M', H_1)$ modular curve over $\mathbb Q$; $K$ carries an $A_0$-algebra structure compatible with $k_0$. The element $j \in K$ has as its Laurent series the coefficientwise image of $j_q$, and is nonzero.
--
--   **Equivariance and group-law data.** The hypotheses `hℓ`, `hM`, `hL` are the variable-change compatibilities required to form $\mathcal R := \mathrm{rigidDataH1Pow}\ A_0\ \ell_g\ M'\ q\ h\ell\ hM\ hL\ \mathcal G\ \mathcal T$: for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$ and variable change $C$, a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-point datum (equation at $(x_P,y_P)$, vanishing of $\mathrm{preΨ}\ \ell_g$ at $x_P$, and $x_Q = x_P$, $y_Q = y_P$) transforms to one for $C \bullet W$; the $\Gamma_0(p^k)$-kernel-polynomial condition `IsGamma0PowAt` is preserved when the polynomial is transformed by `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k)`; and divisibility of $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\ W\ \ell_g\ n\ x$ by $h$ implies divisibility of $\mathrm{inLineMulPoly}\ (C\bullet W)\ \ell_g\ n\ (u^{-2}(x-r))$ by the transformed polynomial. Moreover $\mathcal G$ is a family of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models over $A_0$-algebras with unit discriminant, assumed chord–tangent (`h𝒢`) and with unit section given by the origin chart, where $x/y$ and $z/y$ vanish (`h𝒢O`); $\mathcal T$ is a `LevelTransport` for $\mathcal G$ at $q$, assumed to be a section transport (`h𝒯`). The hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO` provide, for every variable change and every coefficient map of $A_0$-algebras, a graded ring homomorphism between the graded rings of the projective models, dominating the irrelevant ideal and satisfying `IsVariableChangeHom` respectively `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   **The moduli package and the point $x_0$.** $P_0$ is a `LevelModuliPackageAbs` for $\mathcal R.\mathrm{toLevelModuliDatum}$ over $A_0$: a ring $B_0$ with a universal point such that points over any $A_0$-algebra are images of it under a unique $A_0$-algebra map. A point $x_0$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ is given whose $j$-invariant $\mathrm{jOf}\ x_0$ equals, as a Laurent series, $\mathrm{jqNModC}\ k_0\ q$ (`hx₀`). The map $\mathrm{clC} : B_0 \to \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ A_0\ K\ j$ is an $A_0$-algebra map into the chart algebra $\mathrm{chartAlg}\ A_0\ K\ \{j\}$ which, composed with the inclusion into $K$, is the classifying map of $x_0$ (`hclC`).
--
--   **The Tate pin `hμ`.** Writing $\zeta$ for the unit of $k_0$ attached to $\xi$, the hypothesis `hμ` asserts the existence of a variable change $C$ over $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k_0$ and a raw datum $r$ of $\mathcal R$ over $K$ such that: the class of $r$ is $x_0$; the normalisations $u\,(2\,X(\zeta^q) + 6^{-1}) = 2\,Y(\zeta^q) + X(\zeta^q)$, $C.r = -12^{-1}$, $C.s = -2^{-1}$, $C.t = 24^{-1}$ hold, where $(X(\cdot),Y(\cdot)) = \mathrm{tateToricPoint}\ k_0\ q\ (\cdot)$; the curve of $r$, pushed to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k_0$, is $C \bullet \mathrm{tateBase}\ k_0\ q$; for each prime $p \mid M'$, each field $F'$, each ring homomorphism $f : k_0 \to F'$ and each primitive $p^{v_p(M')}$-th root of unity $\zeta' \in F'$, the $\Gamma_0(p^{v_p(M')})$-component $r.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$, pushed to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k_0$ and then reduced coefficientwise by $f$, equals the `kernelVariableChangeDeg` transform by $C.\mathrm{map}(\mathrm{coeffMap}\ f)$ in degree $\mathrm{gamma0PowDeg}\ p\ (v_p(M'))$ of $\prod_{1 \le a \le p^{v_p(M')}/2,\ p \nmid a} (X - (\mathrm{toricPoint}\ F'\ q\ (\zeta'^a))_1)$; the $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-component $r.\mathrm{level}.2.1$, pushed to $\mathrm{LaurentSeries}\ k_0$, is the $C$-variable change of the `LevelPData` with $x_P = x_Q = X(\zeta^q)$ and $y_P = y_Q = Y(\zeta^q)$, where $\zeta^q$ is a primitive $\ell_g$-th root of unity; and there exist $P_x,P_y,Q_x,Q_y \in K$ whose Laurent series are the four coordinates of the $C$-variable change of $\mathrm{cuspData}\ k_0\ q\ (\zeta^{\ell_g})\ (1,0)\ (0,-1)$, with $\mathrm{IsSectionThrough}$ holding for the two Drinfeld sections $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.P$ and $r.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q$ at $(P_x,P_y)$ and $(Q_x,Q_y)$ respectively.
--
--   **Residue comparison.** Finally $\theta : \mathrm{ResidueField}\ A_0 \to \mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ is a ring homomorphism compatible with the residue maps of $A_0$ and $A$ (`hθ`).
--
--   **Conclusion.** Under these hypotheses the following holds for all further data. Let $y$ be a maximal ideal of $\mathrm{chartAlgFin}\ A_0\ K\ j$ and $\psi$ an $A_0$-algebra map from that chart algebra to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A_0$ whose vanishing locus is exactly $y$. Let $x$ be a raw datum of $\mathcal R$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A_0$ whose class is the image of the universal point of $P_0$ under $\psi \circ \mathrm{clC}$, and assume that the affine curve of $x$ has no nonzero $q$-torsion point, i.e. $q \bullet P = 0$ implies $P = 0$.
--
--   Let $\Omega$ be a field that is an algebra over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, let $V$ be a place of $\Omega$ over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, let $\mathrm{res}$ be a ring homomorphism from the residue field of $V$'s valuation subring to $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$, and let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from the chart algebra to $V$'s valuation subring, subject to: $\mathrm{res}$ retracts the structure map of $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$; for $a \in A_0$ the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho(a)$ is the image of $\theta(\mathrm{residue}\ a)$; $\mathrm{res} \circ \mathrm{residue} \circ \rho = \theta \circ \psi$ on the chart algebra; the image in $\Omega$ of $\rho(\mathrm{jChartFin}\ A_0\ K\ j)$ is transcendental over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$; and $\Omega$ is finite-dimensional over the subfield generated over $\mathrm{ResidueField}\ A$ by that element.
--
--   Let $V$'s valuation subring be given an $A_0$-algebra structure, let $\rho_A : B_0 \to V$ be an $A_0$-algebra map with $\rho_A b = \rho(\mathrm{clC}\ b)$ for all $b$, and let $x_V$ be a raw datum of $\mathcal R$ over $V$'s valuation subring whose class is the image of the universal point under $\rho_A$. Let $\chi_Q$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathrm{OriginChartRing}$ of the curve of $x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2$ to $\Omega$ such that $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the inclusion of $V$'s valuation subring into $\Omega$ followed by the section $x_V.\mathrm{level}.2.2.Q$ equals $\mathrm{Spec}\ \chi_Q$ followed by $\mathrm{originChartι}$, and such that $\chi_Q(x/y) = 0$ and $\chi_Q(z/y) = 0$.
--
--   Let $\gamma \in \mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lie in $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$ with $\gamma_{00} \equiv 0$ and $\gamma_{11} \equiv 0 \pmod q$, and let $\tau$ be a $k_0$-algebra automorphism of $K$ with $\mathrm{IsLevelAutAt}\ k_0\ q\ (\xi^{\ell_g})\ q\ (q^2M')\ H_1\ \gamma^{-1}\ K\ \tau$: for all weights $k$, all modular forms $f,g$ of weight $k$ on the group attached to $(q^2M', H_1)$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f, p_g$ where the series of $p_g$ is nonzero, and all $x \in K$ equal to the coefficientwise image of the quotient of these series, and every embedding of $k_0$ into $\mathbb C$ sending $\xi^{\ell_g}$ to $\exp(2\pi i/q)$, the image of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g$ slashed by $\mathrm{conjElemN}\ q\ \gamma^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f$ slashed by the same element. Assume further `hpres`, that $\tau$ maps the chart algebra into itself, and `hTR`, that for every element $h$ of the chart algebra all of whose Laurent coefficients of $\tau h$ lie in the maximal ideal of $A_0$, the image of $\rho h$ in $\Omega$ vanishes.
--
--   Then, for every nonzero $d$ dividing $M'$ such that the element $\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ k_0\ (\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb Q\ d\ j_q)$ lies in $K$ (`hgK`) and lies in the chart algebra (`hgC`), for every algebraically closed field $\Lambda$ that is an $A_0$-algebra, every ring homomorphism $\iota : \Omega \to \Lambda$, every $A_0$-algebra map $\varphi : B_0 \to \Lambda$ with $\varphi b = \iota(\rho_A b)$, with $M' \ne 0$ in $\Lambda$, every raw datum $x_\Lambda$ of $\mathcal R$ over $\Lambda$ whose class is the image of the universal point under $\varphi$, and every point $g$ of the affine curve of $x_\Lambda$ such that $g$ has additive order $M'$ and such that for every prime $p \mid M'$, every $n$ and every nonsingular affine point $(x_1,y_1)$ with $n \bullet g = (x_1,y_1)$ and $\mathrm{addOrderOf}(n \bullet g) = p^{v_p(M')}$ the value $x_1$ is a root of the kernel polynomial $x_\Lambda.\mathrm{level}.1\,p$ (`hg`), one has
--   $$\iota\bigl(\rho(\mathrm{coeffEmb}\ k_0\ (\mathrm{qExpand}\ \mathbb Q\ d\ j_q))\bigr) = \bigl(\mathrm{cyclicQuotientJ}\ x_\Lambda.\mathrm{curve}\ \langle (M'/d)\bullet g\rangle\ d\bigr)^q,$$
--   where the right-hand side is $c_4^3/\Delta$ of the cyclic quotient of the curve of $x_\Lambda$ by the subgroup generated by $(M'/d)\bullet g$ in degree $d$, raised to the $q$-th power.
--
--   At the $H_1$ level with a $\Gamma_1(\ell_g)$-toric Tate pin, this identifies the value at a place of the specialised modular function $j(\mathfrak q^{d})$ with the $q$-th power of the $j$-invariant of the corresponding cyclic quotient, the Frobenius twist being produced by the level automorphism $\tau$ and the congruence conditions on $\gamma$ modulo $q$. It feeds the Frobenius-place statement [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_curve_reduction_eq_map_frobenius_cyclicQuotientJ_eq_of_levelAut_of_originChart_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.Diamond.exists_place_curve_reduction_eq_map_frobenius_cyclicQuotientJ_eq_of_levelAut_of_originChart_rigidDataH1Pow_of_tatePoint_pinGamma1), which compares the reduction of the curve with its Frobenius image.
